text.en:
Ensure approved electrical equipment is received undamaged and installed in the correct location/orientation with compliant anchorage, clearances, environmental protection, physical interfaces and full traceability.
This can include building-side:
panels;
transformers;
disconnects;
cabinets;
motor-control equipment;
distribution boards;
control cabinets;
UPS/battery-related building interfaces;
other approved building electrical equipment.
Specialized substation process equipment may fall outside your building inspection authority.

Verify the physical installation, continuity intent, identification and documented specialist acceptance of grounding/bonding components within the assigned building scope.
This is where your boundary needs to be especially clear.
You can inspect:
physical conductor presence;
routing;
mechanical connection;
bonding jumpers;
equipment grounding interfaces;
visible corrosion/damage;
labeling;
test documentation.
You should not independently certify grounding-system performance unless formally authorized.
